<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Nafin, Cemex set up joint fund.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Nafin, Cemex set up joint fund.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican development bank Nacional Financiera (Nafin) said Monday it had authorised the creation of a joint fund with cement firm Cemex to help finance Cemex's micro-, small- and medium-sized suppliers, clients and distributors.</p>
<p>&quot;With this accord, Cemex will be able to support the strengthening and development of its network of suppliers, made up of 3,000 businesses from around the country, and also promote the modernisation of its distribution network,&quot; Nafin said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not say how much the fund was worth.</p>
<p>--Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289552</p>
